course: dictionary
lesson: 9223
title: Somehow and the hidden how
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Somehow is an adverb. It tells you that something happened, or could happen, even though the writer does not say how. «The Otter knew when people were in trouble they mostly went to Badger, or else Badger got to know of it somehow.» Badger found out, but the text does not tell us the way.
explain: Somehow can also show a feeling with no clear reason. «Somehow I didn't trust him» means you felt it, but you cannot quite explain why. When you see somehow, ask yourself: is the writer hiding the details, or giving me the how?
explain: Look at the words around somehow for clues. «Mole and Badger were sure he would, somehow» means they believed it would happen, even though no plan was given. Swap in your meaning, such as «in some way», and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Maths can hide steps too. «Somehow she got 12» does not show her working, so your job is to find out how she got 12.
fact: Somehow means in some way, although you do not know how or it is hard to explain.
fact: Somehow can mean for some reason that you cannot quite say.
fact: «Somehow or other» means by some way or another, even if it is difficult.
fact: Somehow is an adverb and has no other forms.
exercise: «Toad talks so wonderfully that by the end it's somehow settled.» What does somehow tell us? | It was settled by a loud shout | *It was settled, but the text does not say how | It was settled in a very clear, step-by-step way | It was never settled at all
exercise: Zara's «there's one behind you» was somehow the scariest thing anyone heard all night. Why does the author use somehow? | *The scary feeling has no clear reason we can name | It means the same as very loud | It is a list of other sounds | Zara was asleep when she said it
exercise: «Somehow she got 12.» What must you do in maths? | *Find out how she got 12 | Write 12 with no working at all | Add a second 12 to the answer | Guess an answer and stop there
test: «Somehow or other» means | at the very start of the day | *by some way or another, even if it is difficult | by a rule that is never broken | in a very quiet voice
test: In «Mole and Badger were sure he would, somehow», what feeling is shown? | *They were sure, though no clear plan was given | They had already gone home | They were bored with waiting | They were angry and shouting
exam: Which sentence uses somehow to show that something happened but the way is not given? | *«They reached the top of the hill somehow, though the path was lost.» | «Put the book back on the shelf now.» | «The dog barked very loudly.» | «She ate her lunch at noon.»
